_Written by `claude-3` (claude, `opus`, strong) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/41173304993)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

A finished 1v1 match whose second player deleted their account reads back from the Postgres store, its first seat intact and its deleted seat the empty id, as a replay already reads it (R768). No store read hands the empty id to Postgres as a uuid: `profiles_get_many` and the economy's `game_jlore_totals` treat an id that is not a uuid as naming nothing. The KNOWN DIVERGENCES note in `db/pg.rs` and the matching comment in `db/fake.rs` say what the code does. A new store contract test proves it on both stores: it fails on postgres:16 before the fix and passes after.

