| `crates/server/src/db/fake.rs` | change | doc comment of `remove_profile_rows` only |
| `crates/server/tests/store/contract.rs` | change | new case in `mod profiles`, new case in `mod profiles_remove`, both added to their `both_stores!` lists |

Do not touch `crates/server/src/api/*` (the callers need no change once the store reads are fixed), `crates/server/migrations/`, `spec/`, any `Cargo.toml`, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `bot/`, or any other crate or app. No new ruling: this is store behavior that KNOWN DIVERGENCES (deleted accounts) and R768 already describe. The governing text is migration `crates/server/migrations/0012_account_deletion.sql` (`on delete set null` on a finished match's seats) and `spec/rulings/R0768.md`; R1896000 notes that `matches_seats_filled_unless_over_check` keeps a seat of a live match from emptying. Do not cite any new R-id in a comment.

